# How to cite SpareLine.
# GitHub reads this file and adds a "Cite this repository" button to the
# repository page, with ready-made APA and BibTeX versions.
# Format: Citation File Format 1.2.0 (https://citation-file-format.github.io)

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SpareLine in your work, please cite it using these details."
type: software
title: "SpareLine"
abstract: >-
  SpareLine is a self-hosted backup chat app for organisations. When the usual
  cloud chat, email or meeting tools go down, staff keep talking over the
  office's own network. One office computer runs the server, and staff
  computers find it automatically. Messages are end-to-end encrypted with
  Messaging Layer Security (MLS, RFC 9420), so the server only relays sealed
  messages and administrators cannot read them.

# To credit people by name, replace the entry below with one per person:
